d 【17†Kurt Wiesenfeld】\nL73: \nL74:   * ^{}Physics Department, Brookhaven National Laboratory, Upton, New York 11973\nL75: \nL76: 【18†PDF】\nL77: \nL78: Phys. Rev. Lett. 59, 381 – Published 27 July, 1987\nL79: \nL80: DOI: https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.59.381\nL81: \nL82: [Button: Export Citation]\nL83: \nL84: Show metrics\nL85: ## Abstract\nL86: \nL87: We show that dynamical systems with spatial degrees of freedom naturally evolve into a self-organized critical point. Flicker noise, or 1/f noise, can be identified with the dynamics of the critical state. This picture also yields insight into the origin of fractal objects.\nL88: \nL89: [Button: Close]\nL90: \nL91: [Button: Prev][Button: Next]\nL92: \nL93: ##\nL94: \nL95: 【19†View figure in article】\nL96: \nL97: ## Comments & Replies\nL98: ### 【20†Comment on \"Relaxation at the Angle of Repose\"】\nL99: \nL100: Per Bak, Chao Tang, and Kurt Wiesenfeld\nL101: \nL102: Phys. Rev. Lett. 62, 110 (1989)\nL103: \nL104: # Authorization Required\nL105: \nL106: We need you to provide your credentials before accessing this content.\nL107: \nL108: ## Log in via your institution\nL109: \nL110: If your institution provides access using Shibboleth/OpenAthens log in.\nL111: ## Log in via APS Member Subscription\nL112: \nL113: If you have a personal subscription through your APS membership please log in.\nL114: \nL115: Starting August 1, 2019 APS member subscribers will need to log in using your member credentials instead of your APS Journal Account.\nL116: \nL117: 【21†APS Member Log In】\nL118: \nL119: ## Other Options\nL120: \nL121:   * 【22†Buy Article »】\nL122:   * 【23†Log in with APS Journals Account】\nL123:   * 【24†Log in with username/password provided by your institution】\nL124:   * 【25†Get access through a U.S. public or high school】\nL125: ## 【18†References (Subscription Required)】\nL126: \nL127: [Button: Outline][Button: Information]\nL128: \nL129:   * 【26†Citing Articles (6368)】\nL130:   * 【27†Abstract】\nL131:   * 【28†Com