i Bhabha Road, Bombay 400 005, India\nL74: \nL75: 【16†PDF】\nL76: \nL77: Phys. Rev. Lett. 64, 1613 – Published 2 April, 1990 Erratum 【17†Phys. Rev. Lett. 64, 2837 (1990)】\nL78: \nL79: DOI: https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.64.1613\nL80: \nL81: [Button: Export Citation]\nL82: \nL83: Show metrics\nL84: ## Abstract\nL85: \nL86: We study a general Bak-Tang-Wiesenfeld–type automaton model of self-organized criticality in which the toppling conditions depend on local height, but not on its gradient. We characterize the critical state, and determine its entropy for an arbitrary finite lattice in any dimension. The two-point correlation function is shown to satisfy a linear equation. The spectrum of relaxation times describing the approach to the critical state is also determined exactly.\nL87: \nL88: [Button: Close]\nL89: [Button: Prev][Button: Next]\nL90: ##\nL91: \nL92: 【18†View figure in article】\nL93: \nL94: ## Erratum\nL95: \nL96: ### 【17†Self-Organized Critical State of Sandpile Automation Models】\nL97: \nL98: Deepak Dhar\nL99: \nL100: Phys. Rev. Lett. 64, 2837 (1990)\nL101: \nL102: # Authorization Required\nL103: \nL104: We need you to provide your credentials before accessing this content.\nL105: \nL106: ## Log in via your institution\nL107: \nL108: If your institution provides access using Shibboleth/OpenAthens log in.\nL109: ## Log in via APS Member Subscription\nL110: \nL111: If you have a personal subscription through your APS membership please log in.\nL112: \nL113: Starting August 1, 2019 APS member subscribers will need to log in using your member credentials instead of your APS Journal Account.\nL114: \nL115: 【19†APS Member Log In】\nL116: \nL117: ## Other Options\nL118: \nL119:   * 【20†Buy Article »】\nL120:   * 【21†Log in with APS Journals Account】\nL121:   * 【22†Log in with username/password provided by your institution】\nL122:   * 【23†Get access through a U.S. public or high school】\nL123: ## 【16†References (Subscription Required)】\nL124: \nL125: [Button