ander】\nL74: \nL75:   * ^{}Groupe de Physique de la Matière Condensée, Collège de France, F-75231 Paris, France\nL76: \nL77:   * ^{}Physics Department, University of Michigan, Ann Arbor, Michigan 48109\nL78: \nL79:   * ^{*}Permanent address: Physics Department, University of Michigan, Ann Arbor, Mich. 48109.\nL80: \nL81: 【17†PDF】\nL82: \nL83: Phys. Rev. Lett. 47, 1400 – Published 9 November, 1981\nL84: \nL85: DOI: https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.47.1400\nL86: [Button: Export Citation]\nL87: \nL88: Show metrics\nL89: ## Abstract\nL90: \nL91: A model for random aggregates is studied by computer simulation. The model is applicable to a metal-particle aggregation process whose correlations have been measured previously. Density correlations within the model aggregates fall off with distance with a fractional power law, like those of the metal aggregates. The radius of gyration of the model aggregates has power-law behavior. The model is a limit of a model of dendritic growth.\nL92: \nL93: [Button: Close]\nL94: \nL95: [Button: Prev][Button: Next]\nL96: ##\nL97: \nL98: 【18†View figure in article】\nL99: \nL100: ## Comments & Replies\nL101: \nL102: ### 【19†Crossover of Fractal Dimension in Diffusion-Limited Aggregates】\nL103: \nL104: D. Bensimon, E. Domany, and A. Aharony\nL105: \nL106: Phys. Rev. Lett. 51, 1394 (1983)\nL107: \nL108: # Authorization Required\nL109: \nL110: We need you to provide your credentials before accessing this content.\nL111: \nL112: ## Log in via your institution\nL113: \nL114: If your institution provides access using Shibboleth/OpenAthens log in.\nL115: ## Log in via APS Member Subscription\nL116: \nL117: If you have a personal subscription through your APS membership please log in.\nL118: \nL119: Starting August 1, 2019 APS member subscribers will need to log in using your member credentials instead of your APS Journal Account.\nL120: \nL121: 【20†APS Member Log In】\nL122: \nL123: ## Other Options\nL124: \nL125:   * 【21†Buy Article »】\nL126:  